
@startuml

' ============================================================================
' PROXY DESIGN PATTERN — DIGITAL LIBRARY (C++17)
' ============================================================================

title Proxy Design Pattern — Digital Library (C++17)

left to right direction

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho


' ============================================================================
' 1. SUBJECT INTERFACE
' ============================================================================

abstract class IBook <<Subject>> {
    + {abstract} getTitle() : std::string_view
    + {abstract} getAuthor() : std::string_view
    + {abstract} getContent() : std::string_view
    + ~IBook()
}


' ============================================================================
' 2. REAL SUBJECT
' ============================================================================

class Book <<RealSubject>> {
    - title_ : std::string
    - author_ : std::string
    - content_ : std::string
    --
    + Book(title : std::string, author : std::string)
    + getTitle() : std::string_view
    + getAuthor() : std::string_view
    + getContent() : std::string_view
}


' ============================================================================
' 3. PROXY
' ============================================================================

class BookProxy <<Proxy>> {
    - title_ : std::string
    - author_ : std::string
    - role_ : UserRole
    - realBook_ : std::unique_ptr<Book>
    --
    - authorizeRead() : void
    - ensureLoaded() : void
    --
    + BookProxy(title : std::string, author : std::string, role : UserRole)
    + getTitle() : std::string_view
    + getAuthor() : std::string_view
    + getContent() : std::string_view
}


' ============================================================================
' 4. ACCESS-CONTROL CONTEXT
' ============================================================================

enum UserRole {
    Guest
    Member
}


' ============================================================================
' 5. CLIENT
' ============================================================================

class "main()" as Client <<Client>>


' ============================================================================
' 6. RELATIONSHIPS
' ============================================================================

' Both implementations share the same Subject interface.
IBook <|-- Book
IBook <|-- BookProxy

' The Proxy exclusively owns the RealSubject.
' Multiplicity 0..1 represents lazy initialization.
BookProxy "1" *-- "0..1" Book : owns / creates lazily

' The Proxy stores a user role for authorization.
BookProxy --> UserRole : checks role

' The Client constructs concrete proxies.
Client ..> BookProxy : creates

' The Client uses the shared Subject interface.
' Polymorphic access is explained in the Client note.
Client ..> IBook


' ============================================================================
' 7. DESIGN NOTES
' ============================================================================

note bottom of BookProxy
  Virtual Proxy:
  - Defers construction of Book.
  - Reuses the existing instance.
  - Provides metadata without loading.

  Protection Proxy:
  - Checks UserRole before loading.
  - Rejects unauthorized requests.

  Content access:
  1. authorizeRead()
  2. ensureLoaded()
  3. realBook_->getContent()
end note

note bottom of Book
  RealSubject:
  - Stores title, author, and content.
  - Initializes content during construction.
  - Returns non-owning string_view values.

  Content loading is simulated using
  a fixed description of "1984".
end note

note bottom of Client
  Demonstrates:
  - Member access
  - Guest access
  - Lazy initialization
  - Object reuse
  - Polymorphic access via IBook&

  main() is a function, represented
  as a class-shaped client for UML.
end note

@enduml
